    "plotType": "Linearized scatter with fit line (ln k vs. 1/T)",
    "description": "An Arrhenius plot linearizes reaction-rate data by graphing the natural log of the rate constant against the reciprocal of absolute temperature. Because the Arrhenius equation predicts ln k = ln A − (Ea/R)(1/T), the data fall on a straight line whose slope encodes the activation energy. It is the standard way chemists extract Ea and the pre-exponential factor from rate measurements taken at several temperatures.",
